 R←Test_API_036(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;buff;res
⍝ Runs "ChangeLog" against a repository without any commits. Git says "does not have any commits
⍝ yet", and that path used to return an empty VECTOR although the leading comment promises a
⍝ matrix with four columns.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (rc msg buff)←tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'init'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 (⊂' r←Foo' ' r←1')⎕NPUT tempDir,'/Foo.aplf'

 res←tempDir G.ChangeLog tempDir,'/Foo.aplf'   ⍝ Absolute, so no project is needed
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠⍴⍴res
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0 4≢⍴res

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
